This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 to simulate a clean energy monitoring system using the gpiozero library. It initializes GPIO17 and GPIO4 as simulated input pins, reads the Raspberry Pi's internal temperature, simulates sensor readings for light level, temperature, voltage, and current, and logs the data with timestamps. It also triggers threshold actions based on the sensor readings and handles graceful shutdown on keyboard interrupt.

